# `console/docker-entrypoint.sh` runs under /bin/sh in a Linux container. A
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true — the Windows default, and this repository is
# developed on Windows — would give it CRLF line endings, which /bin/sh reports
# as a bad interpreter or, more confusingly, carries into the middle of a path.
# The Dockerfile strips them defensively as well; this is the half that keeps
# the committed bytes right in the first place.
*.sh text eol=lf
